(5419329, 777921, 32011, '<td valign="top">This is an excellent capture.  I imagine it took a bit of planning, and a lot of patience to get this one.  You''ve done well.<br/> <br/>Now that my comment about your photo is done... please bear with me... I''m conducting a little comment experiment... something like <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=97166" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">K10DGuy</a>''s comments, but with a twist... the twist being, the story will move from one photo to another within the challenge.<br/> <br/>Yours is the 4th in the sequence... :<br/> <br/>------------------<br/>=== <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/challenge_vote_image.php?IMAGE_ID=769675" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">previous</a> ===<br/> <br/>Ivan and Boris emerged from the subway station and were amazed at how empty the city was.  They were soon joined by another man, Sergei.  The three men roamed the city looking for signs of life... but there were none to be found.  They were alone.  What had become of their families, their friends?  Where had all the animals gone?<br/> <br/>=== <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/challenge_vote_image.php?IMAGE_ID=778324" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">next</a> ===</td>', 'This is an excellent capture.  I imagine it took a bit of planning, and a lot of patience to get this one.  You''ve done well. Now that my comment about your photo is done... please bear with me... I''m conducting a little comment experiment... something like  K10DGuy''s comments, but with a twist... the twist being, the story will move from one photo to another within the challenge. Yours is the 4th in the sequence... : ------------------=== previous === Ivan and Boris emerged from the subway station and were amazed at how empty the city was.  They were soon joined by another man, Sergei.  The three men roamed the city looking for signs of life... but there were none to be found.  They were alone.  What had become of their families, their friends?  Where had all the animals gone? === next ===', '2009-04-05 08:09:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(5419330, 778324, 32011, '<td valign="top">This is an absolutely breathtaking image.  The balance of sky and ice, cloud and clear sky... brilliant... and the colours are perfect.  Exceptional!<br/> <br/> <br/>Now that my comment about your photo is done... please bear with me... I''m conducting a little comment experiment... something like <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=97166" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">K10DGuy</a>''s comments, but with a twist... the twist being, the story will move from one photo to another within the challenge.<br/> <br/>Yours is the 5th in the sequence... :<br/> <br/>------------------<br/>=== <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/challenge_vote_image.php?IMAGE_ID=777921" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">previous</a> ===<br/> <br/>The three men roamed to earth looking for signs of life.  No man, nor woman.  No animal.  No plant.  There was nothing left, but the three of them.  "Are we the meek that are to inherit the Earth" Boris asked.  "What sort of inheritance is this?  We have no food?  We have nothing?" Sergei cried.  It was getting cold and the trio hadn''t found any signs of life in their own area, so they decided to head south, where it was warmer and they might find some food.<br/> <br/>=== <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/challenge_vote_image.php?IMAGE_ID=778461" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">next</a> ===</td>', 'This is an absolutely breathtaking image.  The balance of sky and ice, cloud and clear sky... brilliant... and the colours are perfect.  Exceptional!  Now that my comment about your photo is done... please bear with me... I''m conducting a little comment experiment... something like  K10DGuy''s comments, but with a twist... the twist being, the story will move from one photo to another within the challenge. Yours is the 5th in the sequence... : ------------------=== previous === The three men roamed to earth looking for signs of life.  No man, nor woman.  No animal.  No plant.  There was nothing left, but the three of them.  "Are we the meek that are to inherit the Earth" Boris asked.  "What sort of inheritance is this?  We have no food?  We have nothing?" Sergei cried.  It was getting cold and the trio hadn''t found any signs of life in their own area, so they decided to head south, where it was warmer and they might find some food. === next ===', '2009-04-05 08:09:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(5419331, 778461, 32011, '<td valign="top">This is so simple, yet so stunning.  Great tones, detail and composition.  One of my favourites in the challenge.<br/> <br/> <br/>Now that my comment about your photo is done... please bear with me while I use your image in a little comment experiment... something like <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=97166" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">K10DGuy</a>''s comments, but with a twist... the twist being, the story will move from one photo to another within the challenge.<br/> <br/> <br/>Yours is the sixth in the sequence... :<br/> <br/>------------------<br/>=== <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/challenge_vote_image.php?IMAGE_ID=778324" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">previous</a> ===<br/> <br/>The three ventured south... FAR south... but found nobody.  They did manage to find the occasional pieces of vegetation, which they shared... however, they were tiring.  They decided to take shelter from the sun in a cave and rest before they continued their trek to find others.<br/> <br/>=== <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/challenge_vote_image.php?IMAGE_ID=778062" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">next</a> ===</td>', 'This is so simple, yet so stunning.  Great tones, detail and composition.  One of my favourites in the challenge.  Now that my comment about your photo is done... please bear with me while I use your image in a little comment experiment... something like  K10DGuy''s comments, but with a twist... the twist being, the story will move from one photo to another within the challenge.  Yours is the sixth in the sequence... : ------------------=== previous === The three ventured south... FAR south... but found nobody.  They did manage to find the occasional pieces of vegetation, which they shared... however, they were tiring.  They decided to take shelter from the sun in a cave and rest before they continued their trek to find others. === next ===', '2009-04-05 08:09:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(5419332, 778062, 32011, '<td valign="top">Well composed.  Nice and sharp.  Would have liked it to be a bit darker, which would have added a tad more drama to it.  I find the wires and the orange twig(?) very distracting... could have used a tighter crop and convert it to B&amp;W perhaps.  Overall though, a good image.<br/> <br/> <br/>Now that my comment about your photo is done... please bear with me while I use your image in a little comment experiment... something like <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=97166" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">K10DGuy</a>''s comments, but with a twist... the twist being, the story will move from one photo to another within the challenge.<br/> <br/> <br/>Yours is the seventh and final in the sequence... :<br/> <br/>------------------<br/>=== <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/challenge_vote_image.php?IMAGE_ID=778461" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">previous</a> ===<br/> <br/>The three rested in the cave.  For the first time since they found themselves alone in the world, they found sleep easily that evening.  Sleep comes easily to those with no worries, and those that have given up all hope have no worries in the world.  They slept, and they never woke... now the world was empty... now the meek could inherit the Earth.<br/> <br/>=== THE END ===</td>', 'Well composed.  Nice and sharp.  Would have liked it to be a bit darker, which would have added a tad more drama to it.  I find the wires and the orange twig(?) very distracting... could have used a tighter crop and convert it to B&W perhaps.  Overall though, a good image.  Now that my comment about your photo is done... please bear with me while I use your image in a little comment experiment... something like  K10DGuy''s comments, but with a twist... the twist being, the story will move from one photo to another within the challenge.  Yours is the seventh and final in the sequence... : ------------------=== previous === The three rested in the cave.  For the first time since they found themselves alone in the world, they found sleep easily that evening.  Sleep comes easily to those with no worries, and those that have given up all hope have no worries in the world.  They slept, and they never woke... now the world was empty... now the meek could inherit the Earth. === THE END ===', '2009-04-05 08:09:48.000000', NULL, 1),
